  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Help save the jaguar in the Yucatan Peninsula</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2004, our project has focused on gathering information about local population status, protecting important areas of the Jaguar, and minimizing conflicts with ranchers.  - For 19 years we&apos;ve been studying the natural history of jaguars and their prey to ensure their protection and identify their priority areas.  - Protecting Jaguars lets us save much more species in tropical forests and preserve the ecosystem services they provide directly and indirectly to humans and nature.</narrative>
  </description>
